# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# The chunk archive deploy_frontend.sh keeps so open tabs survive a deploy.
#
# Ignored for a reason that is not about git. Tailwind v4's scanner skips what
# .gitignore skips — which is how it never reads `.next` — and this directory
# was the one build artefact it was still allowed to read. It holds old
# compiled CSS chunks and woff2 fonts, so the scanner pulled class candidates
# out of minified CSS and binary font data — selectors carrying a U+FFFD
# replacement character and a raw 0x01 byte, twenty-seven of them.
#
# Harmless until production, where Tailwind runs the output through Lightning
# CSS, which refuses a control byte in a selector. The build then fails as
# `globals.css: Missed semicolon` — a file that is perfectly valid — while
# `npm run dev` and every local build stay green, because neither optimises.
.static-archive/
.next.*
